From: Plain Browser
Subject: [hooks] ChromeContentBrowserClient: one hook per extension point

Category: 20-hooks. Browser-side extension points of ChromeContentBrowserClient, through //plainbrowser/hooks/browser_hooks.h:
ExposeInterfacesToRenderer (chrome_content_browser_client_receiver_bindings.cc: our mojo interfaces for a new
renderer process), AppendRendererCommandLineSwitches (per-renderer switches: fingerprint session key, initial
exception list), AddNavigationThrottles (our navigation throttles). A new feature adds itself in
src/plainbrowser/hooks and never changes this patch.
---
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
 // found in the LICENSE file.
 
 #include "chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.h"
+
+// Plain Browser: own includes (patches/series), kept together up here so that
+// changes to the upstream include list below never touch this hunk.
+#include "plainbrowser/hooks/browser_hooks.h"
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <iterator>
@@ -3158,6 +3162,9 @@
 #endif
 
